        "title": "Sugar Crops - Sugarcane, Sugar Beet, and the Sweetness Economy",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Sugar went from luxury to commodity to ubiquitous food additive in 400 years. In 1700, European per-capita sugar consumption was ~2 kg/year (expensive luxury). By 2000, it was ~40 kg/year. This transformation required: (1) Caribbean plantation slavery, (2) sugar beet to break the monopoly, and (3) high-fructose corn syrup to make sweetness cheap at industrial scale. Each step reshaped geopolitics."
    },
