      "text": "SUGAR TIMELINE\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\n~8,000 BP   Sugarcane domesticated in New Guinea (chewed raw)\n~500 BCE    India: crystallized sugar production (kanda = candy)\n~600 CE     Arab traders spread sugar refining across Middle East/Mediterranean\n1493        Columbus brings sugarcane to Hispaniola\n1501        First enslaved Africans in Caribbean sugar plantations\n1600-1800   Triangle trade: sugar economy → 12M enslaved Africans transported\n~1700       Europe: sugar = luxury, ~2 kg/capita/year\n1747        Andreas Marggraf: sugar found in beet root\n1801        First commercial beet sugar factory (Cunern, Silesia)\n1806        Napoleon's Continental Blockade → forces beet sugar expansion\n1807        British abolition of slave trade\n1834        British emancipation (West Indies) → Caribbean sugar cost rises\n1843        Mechanical vacuum pan crystallization → mass production\n1879        Saccharin discovered (Constantin Fahlberg)\n1930s       Ion exchange resin refining → purer sugar\n1957        R.O. Marshall: glucose isomerase converts glucose → fructose\n1970        HFCS commercial production begins\n1975        HFCS 55 mainstream in US soft drinks (Coca-Cola switches ~1980)\n2000        US sugar consumption: ~40 kg/capita/year\n```"
